Project Brief: SentientShield EDR Implementation
Duration: 1 week to  4 Week (Intensive Phase)
Core Technologies: Wazuh (Manager & Indexer), Sysmon, Atomic Red Team, Docker, Kali Linux.

Week 1: Infrastructure & Agent Deployment
The foundation of the EDR was established using a containerized architecture to ensure scalability and isolation.

Wazuh Manager Deployment: Set up a Dockerized Wazuh central manager and indexer to handle log ingestion and alerting.

Multi-OS Enrollment: Successfully enrolled both Linux (Kali) and Windows agents into the environment.

Deep Visibility: Integrated Microsoft Sysmon on Windows endpoints to capture granular process-level telemetry that standard OS logs miss.

Heartbeat Verification: Validated the secure communication channel (AES encryption) between agents and the manager.

Week 2: Configuration & Advanced Detection
Shifted focus from connectivity to data quality and visibility depth.

File Integrity Monitoring (FIM): Configured real-time monitoring for sensitive system directories (/etc, /bin, C:\Windows\System32) to detect unauthorized changes.

Vulnerability Detection: Enabled the Wazuh Vulnerability Detector to cross-reference installed software versions against the CVE database.

System Inventory: Automated the collection of hardware specs, installed packages, and open ports for comprehensive asset management.

Week 3: Active Response & IPS Implementation
Transformed the system from a passive observer to an Active Response defender.

IPS Integration: Configured an automated firewall-drop response. When the manager detected an SSH brute-force attack (Rule 5712), it dynamically updated the agent's firewall to block the attacker.

Attack Validation: Manually simulated SSH attacks from a separate Kali instance and verified the "Connection Refused" status, proving the EDR’s autonomous remediation capabilities.

Web & Rootkit Defense: Tested triggers for SQL Injection attempts and hidden system files (Rule 510).

Week 4: Threat Simulation & Kill Chain Mapping
Finalized the project by validating the EDR against professional-grade adversary techniques.

Adversary Emulation: Deployed the Atomic Red Team (ART) framework on the Lead-kali-EDR agent.

Ransomware Simulation: Executed MITRE Technique T1070.002 (Indicator Removal) to simulate the log-clearing behavior typical of ransomware variants.

MITRE ATT&CK Mapping: Successfully mapped raw alerts to the MITRE ATT&CK Heatmap.

Kill Chain Visualization: Presented a full "Kill Chain" in the dashboard, showing the progression from Initial Access (Execution) to the Impact (Log Destruction).

Final Security Posture Summary
The SentientShield EDR is now a fully realized security operations center (SOC) in a box. It successfully demonstrates the three pillars of modern cybersecurity:

Visibility: Knowing exactly what is happening on every endpoint.

Detection: Identifying malicious patterns using a mix of signatures and behavioral analysis.

Remediation: Automatically stopping threats before they can cause permanent damage.
